@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle
hide methods
left to right direction

package "USEI10: Radius Search Engine" {

    class TrainStation {
        +stationId
        +station
        +country
        +latitude
        +longitude
        +isCity
    }

    class TrainStationLoader {
        +load()
    }

    class KDTreeStations {
        +root
        +buildFromStations()
        +rangeSearch()
    }

    class StationDistance {
        +station
        +distanceKm
    }

    class DistanceNameKey {
        +distance
        +stationName
        +seq
    }

    class AVLTree {
        +insert()
        +inOrder()
    }

    class USEI10Controller {
        +radiusSearch()
        -haversineKm()
    }

    class Result {
        +tree
        +countByCountry
        +countByIsCity
        +totalIndexedStations
        +matchedCount
    }

    class USEI10UI {
        +readInputs()
        +displayResults()
    }
}

' RELATIONSHIPS

USEI10UI --> USEI10Controller : invokes >
USEI10Controller --> TrainStationLoader : loads stations >
USEI10Controller --> KDTreeStations : builds KD-tree >
KDTreeStations --> TrainStation : contains >
USEI10Controller --> StationDistance : creates >
USEI10Controller --> DistanceNameKey : builds AVL keys >
USEI10Controller --> AVLTree : inserts sorted results >
USEI10Controller --> Result : returns >
Result --> TrainStation : contains >
Result --> DistanceNameKey : ordered by >

' NOTES

note right of KDTreeStations
KD-Tree performs spatial pruning
using a rectangular bounding box:
lat ∈ [min,max], lon ∈ [min,max].
Only candidates in this box are visited.
end note

note bottom of USEI10Controller
USEI10 workflow:
1. Load CSV dataset
2. Build KD-tree from stations
3. Compute bounding-box for circle
4. KD-tree rangeSearch retrieves candidates
5. Exact Haversine filter for radius
6. Sort by (distance ASC, name DESC)
7. Insert into AVLTree
8. Compute summaries (country, isCity)
end note

note right of DistanceNameKey
Composite AVL key:
1. distance (ASC)
2. stationName (DESC)
3. seq (ASC)
Ensures strict ordering
and uniqueness inside AVL.
end note

note bottom of AVLTree
AVL maintains stable ordering:
inOrder traversal = final result
sorted deterministically.
end note

note bottom of USEI10UI
UI only orchestrates:
- reads inputs
- calls controller
- prints ordered results
- prints summaries
- prints complexity O(log N + k log k)
end note

@enduml
